### 14.6 Box Generation Spec Compliance
Fix CssBoxTree.Generate_Tree() and Generate_Box() to comply with W3C CSS Display 3 and CSS 2.2.
Spec Reference: https://www.w3.org/TR/css-display-3/#box-generation
Spec Reference: https://www.w3.org/TR/CSS22/visuren.html#box-gen

#### 14.6.0 Box Tree Regeneration Bug Fixes ✓

#### 14.6.1 Anonymous Block Box Generation (CSS 2.2 §9.2.1.1) ✓

#### 14.6.2 display: contents Support (CSS Display 3 §2.5) ✓
- [x] display: contents computes to display: none for replaced elements (IsReplacedElement check in Display_Computed resolver)

#### 14.6.3 Text Sequence Handling (CSS Display 3 §1) ✓
Box generation for text sequences is complete. Per CSS Display 3 §1:
- Empty text nodes (zero characters) do NOT generate text sequences ✓
- Whitespace-only text nodes DO generate text sequences (whitespace is text content) ✓
- Contiguous sibling text nodes are combined into a single text sequence ✓
Note: Whitespace collapsing/trimming is controlled by the white-space property during
inline formatting context layout (phase 18.3), not during box generation.
- [x] Empty text nodes generate no box
- [x] Whitespace-only text nodes generate text run (correct per spec)
- [x] Documented future white-space property dependency in code comments

#### 14.6.4 List Item Marker Boxes (CSS Display 3 §2.3) ✓
display: list-item generates principal box + ::marker pseudo-element.
- [x] Detect EDisplayMode.LIST_ITEM in Generate_Box()
- [x] Generate marker box in addition to principal box
- [x] Position marker box according to list-style-position
- [x] Marker content from list-style-type property
- [x] Tests for list-item marker generation (43 tests)

#### 14.6.5 Table Internal Box Fixup (CSS Display 3 §2.4, CSS 2.2 §17.2) ✓
Table cells/rows in wrong parent generate anonymous wrapper boxes.
- [x] Detect table-internal display types (table-cell, table-row, etc.)
- [x] Generate anonymous table-row around orphaned table-cell
- [x] Generate anonymous table-row-group around orphaned table-row
- [x] Generate anonymous table around orphaned table-row-group
- [x] Chain all necessary wrappers (cell → row → row-group → table)
- [x] Tests for table anonymous box generation (35 tests)

#### 14.6.6 Automatic Box Type Transformations (CSS Display 3 §2.7) ✓
Blockification/inlinification based on position/float/parent context.
- [ ] Blockify floated elements (float != none → outer display: block) — requires Phase 15
- [x] Blockify absolutely/fixed positioned elements
- [x] Blockify children of flex/grid containers
- [ ] Inlinify children of ruby containers
- [x] Apply transformations during cascade (Display_Computed resolver)
- [x] Tests for blockification scenarios (5 tests passing)

#### 14.6.7 Run-In Boxes (CSS Display 3 §5) — DEFERRED ⊗
**Status:** Deferred indefinitely due to spec instability and minimal browser support.
- [x] Documented rationale for deferral
- [x] Added code comments explaining at-risk status
- [x] Created test documenting deferred status
- [x] Verified parser recognizes display: run-in

**Rationale:**
- CSS Display Level 3 marks 'display: run-in' as **"at-risk"**, meaning the CSS WG believes
  it "may have difficulty being interoperably implemented in a timely manner"
- The spec explicitly allows this feature to be dropped without publishing a new CR
- Browser support: None (Chrome/Firefox/Safari all removed support)
- Complex implementation: Requires post-generation tree manipulation and special ::first-letter handling
- EDisplayMode.RUN_IN enum value exists for parser compatibility but generates no special boxes

**If implementing in future:**
- [ ] Detect display: run-in and inlinify contents (if inner type is 'flow')
- [ ] Detect run-in sequences (maximal consecutive siblings + intervening whitespace/out-of-flow)
- [ ] If followed by block box that doesn't establish BFC, reparent run-in as first inline child (after ::marker, before ::before)
- [ ] Otherwise generate anonymous block wrapper around run-in sequence
- [ ] Handle ::first-letter interaction (run-in provides first letter to containing block)
- [ ] Tests for basic/orphaned/multiple run-ins, BFC boundary prevention

#### 14.6.8 Multiple Box Generation ✓
Table elements generate multiple boxes per CSS Display 3 §2.2.
- [x] Create CssTableWrapperBox class (inherits from CssPrincipalBox)
- [x] Create CssTableGridBox class (inherits from CssBox)
- [x] Detect display:table in Generate_Box() and call Generate_Table_Boxes()
- [x] Generate table wrapper box (principal) + grid box (child)
- [x] Add Get_Container_Box() helper to route table children to grid box
- [x] Override DisplayType in CssTableWrapperBox to return Flow_Root
- [x] Handle box tree child transfer (skip grid box during regeneration)
- [x] Tests for table wrapper+grid generation (16 tests passing)
  - Table generates wrapper box with correct type
  - Wrapper contains grid box as child
  - Grid box has table inner display type
  - Children are added to grid box, not wrapper
  - Multiple children all routed to grid box
  - Box tree structure is correct
  - Originating element references work
  - Non-table elements unaffected
