## Phase 16: Margin Collapsing
Spec Reference: https://www.w3.org/TR/CSS2/box.html#collapsing-margins
Prerequisites: Phase 14 (Layout Pipeline Integration)

### 16.1 Margin Collapse Detection ✓
Implement adjoining margin detection per CSS 2.2 §8.3.1.
- [x] Add MarginCollapseState tracking to BlockFormattingContext
- [x] Detect adjacent sibling margins (vertical only)
- [x] Detect parent/first-child margin adjacency
- [x] Detect parent/last-child margin adjacency
- [x] Detect empty block margins (top meets bottom)

**Implementation Complete:**
- MarginCollapseState class with positive/negative margin tracking
- CalculateCollapsedMargin() implementing CSS 2.2 collapse algorithm
- IsTopMarginAdjoining() and IsBottomMarginAdjoining() adjacency checks
- HandleAdjacentSiblingCollapse() for sibling collapse detection
- HandleParentFirstChildCollapse() for parent/first-child detection
- HandleParentLastChildCollapse() for parent/last-child detection
- IsEmptyBox() for detecting empty blocks where margins collapse through
- Proper handling of floats, absolutely positioned, and cleared elements

### 16.2 Margin Collapse Calculation
- [ ] Calculate collapsed margin = max(margin1, margin2) for positive
- [ ] Handle negative margins: most negative wins
- [ ] Handle mixed positive/negative: max(positive) + min(negative)
- [ ] Track collapsed margin through to positioning

### 16.3 Margin Collapse Prevention
Margins don't collapse in certain cases:
- [ ] Floats don't collapse with anything
- [ ] Absolutely/fixed positioned elements don't collapse
- [ ] Inline-block elements don't collapse
- [ ] Elements with overflow != visible don't collapse (create new BFC)
- [ ] Elements with padding/border between margins don't collapse

### 16.4 Margin Collapsing Tests
