## Phase 26: Logical Pseudo-Class Selectors
Spec Reference: https://www.w3.org/TR/selectors-4/#logical-combination
Prerequisites: Phase 11.9.1 (Nesting Selector complete)

### 26.1 :is() Pseudo-Class (16 tests blocked)
The `:is()` pseudo-class matches any element that matches one of the selectors in its argument list.
- [ ] Implement `PseudoClassSelectorIs` in CSS/Selector/Types/
- [ ] Parse selector list argument using existing `SelectorParser`
- [ ] Match returns true if element matches ANY selector in the list
- [ ] Forgiving selector list: invalid selectors are ignored, not entire selector
- [ ] Specificity: takes the HIGHEST specificity of any argument
- [ ] Update `PseudoClassSelector.Create_Function()` to dispatch "is"
- [ ] Add tests for :is() matching and specificity

### 26.2 :where() Pseudo-Class
Similar to `:is()` but with ZERO specificity contribution.
- [ ] Implement `PseudoClassSelectorWhere` in CSS/Selector/Types/
- [ ] Same matching logic as :is()
- [ ] Specificity: always contributes (0,0,0) regardless of arguments
- [ ] Forgiving selector list behavior
- [ ] Update `PseudoClassSelector.Create_Function()` to dispatch "where"
- [ ] Add tests for :where() matching and specificity

### 26.3 :has() Pseudo-Class (Relational)
Matches elements that have descendants/siblings matching the argument.
Prerequisites: 26.1 (:is() as reference implementation)
- [ ] Implement `PseudoClassSelectorHas` in CSS/Selector/Types/
- [ ] Support relative selectors (>, +, ~) in argument
- [ ] Match requires walking DOM tree to find matching descendants
- [ ] Performance consideration: may need to cache results
- [ ] Subject invalidation when DOM changes
- [ ] Add tests for :has() with various combinators

### 26.4 Enhanced :not() Specificity
Bug: :not() currently counts as single pseudo-class instead of argument's specificity.
- [ ] Fix `PseudoClassSelectorNot.Get_Specificity()` to return argument's specificity
- [ ] Handle multiple selectors: :not(.a, .b) takes highest specificity
- [ ] Add test: `Not_SpecificityCalculation` (currently skipped)

## Phase 27: Form/Input Pseudo-Class Selectors
Spec Reference: https://www.w3.org/TR/selectors-4/#ui-pseudos
Prerequisites: Phase 19 (HTML Form Elements)

### 27.1 Form Element Infrastructure
Prerequisites: Phase 19 (HTML Form Elements)
- [ ] Verify `HTMLInputElement` has `disabled`, `checked`, `required` properties
- [ ] Verify `HTMLButtonElement` has `disabled` property
- [ ] Verify `HTMLSelectElement` has `disabled` property
- [ ] Verify `HTMLTextAreaElement` has `disabled`, `required` properties
- [ ] Add `IFormAssociatedElement` interface if not present
- [ ] Ensure `validity` state object exists for validation pseudo-classes

### 27.2 Enabled/Disabled State (6 tests blocked)
- [ ] Implement `:enabled` matching in `PseudoClassSelector.Matches()`
  - Returns true for form elements that are NOT disabled
  - Must check parent fieldset disabled state
- [ ] Implement `:disabled` matching
  - Returns true for form elements with `disabled` attribute
  - Or within disabled fieldset
- [ ] Only applies to form-associated elements
- [ ] Add tests for :enabled/:disabled

### 27.3 Checked/Indeterminate State (6 tests blocked)
Prerequisites: 27.1 (Form Element Infrastructure)
- [ ] Implement `:checked` matching
  - checkbox/radio inputs with `checked` property true
  - option elements that are selected
- [ ] Implement `:indeterminate` matching
  - checkbox with `indeterminate` property true
  - radio buttons with no selection in group
  - progress elements with no value
- [ ] Add tests for :checked/:indeterminate

### 27.4 Validity State (12 tests blocked)
Prerequisites: 27.1 (Form Element Infrastructure), HTMLInputElement.validity
- [ ] Implement `:valid` matching
  - Form elements that satisfy validation constraints
- [ ] Implement `:invalid` matching
  - Form elements that do NOT satisfy validation constraints
- [ ] Implement `:required` / `:optional` matching
  - Based on `required` attribute
- [ ] Implement `:in-range` / `:out-of-range` matching
  - For number/date inputs with min/max
- [ ] Add tests for validation pseudo-classes

### 27.5 Read/Write State (4 tests blocked)
Prerequisites: 27.1 (Form Element Infrastructure)
- [ ] Implement `:read-only` matching
  - readonly attribute OR not an editable element
- [ ] Implement `:read-write` matching
  - Editable inputs/textareas without readonly
  - contenteditable elements
- [ ] Add tests for :read-only/:read-write

### 27.6 Placeholder/Default State (4 tests blocked)
Prerequisites: 27.1 (Form Element Infrastructure)
- [ ] Implement `:placeholder-shown` matching
  - Input/textarea showing placeholder text
- [ ] Implement `:default` matching
  - Default button in form
  - Default option in select
  - Checked checkbox/radio with checked attribute
- [ ] Add tests for :placeholder-shown/:default

### 27.7 Focus State (8 tests blocked)
Prerequisites: Phase 20 (Event System)
- [ ] Implement `:focus` matching
  - Element is the current focus target
- [ ] Implement `:focus-within` matching
  - Element or descendant has focus
- [ ] Implement `:focus-visible` matching
  - Focus should be visibly indicated (keyboard navigation)
